# Sinux installer - English catalog
# Lines are KEY=VALUE. \n is expanded by printf %b at runtime.
APP_TITLE=Sinux Installer 1.1.0
INTRO=Welcome to the Sinux terminal installer.\n\nThis boot media is a minimal Linux live system used ONLY as an installer vehicle.\nWhat gets installed on your disk is the Sinux kernel (a terminal-only, from-scratch OS).\n\nThe target disk will be completely ERASED. A GPT layout bootable by BOTH BIOS and UEFI will be created.\nSecure Boot must be disabled on real hardware.
ABOUT_TITLE=About
ABOUT_TEXT=Sinux Installer 1.1.0\n\nUpstream project: github.com/SinuxProject/Sinux\nInstalled kernel: Sinux x86_64 Multiboot2 (built from source, terminal shell only)\nInstaller live OS: Debian 13 minimal Linux, text mode only\nDisk layout: GPT / 1 MiB BIOS-boot + 128 MiB EFI FAT32 + ext2 root\nBoot support: legacy BIOS (i386-pc) and UEFI x86_64 (removable path)\n\nThis installer is bilingual: choose English or Farsi at the boot menu.
MAIN_TITLE=Sinux Installer - main menu
MAIN_TEXT=Select an action with the arrow keys, then press Enter.
ACT_INSTALL=Install Sinux to a disk
ACT_LANG=Change language / تغییر زبان
ACT_RESCUE=Open a rescue shell
ACT_REBOOT=Reboot the machine
ACT_POWEROFF=Power off the machine
ACT_ABOUT=About this installer
ACT_EXIT=Exit installer (drop to shell)
LANG_TITLE=Language / زبان
LANG_TEXT=Choose the installer language.
LANG_EN=English
LANG_FA=فارسی (Farsi)
DISK_TITLE=Select target disk
DISK_TEXT=Choose the disk that will be WIPED and turned into a Sinux system.
NO_DISK=No suitable disk was found. Check that the storage driver is loaded, then use the rescue shell.
WARN_TITLE=WARNING - DATA LOSS
WARN_TEXT=ALL DATA on the selected disk will be DESTROYED.\n\nThe disk will be repartitioned as GPT with three partitions:\n  1  1 MiB   BIOS boot partition\n  2  128 MiB EFI System Partition (FAT32)\n  3  rest    Sinux root (ext2 by default)\n\nThis cannot be undone.
CONFIRM_TITLE=Confirm disk
CONFIRM_TEXT=Type the exact disk name to confirm (for example: sda or nvme0n1).
CONFIRM_BAD=The typed name did not match. Nothing was changed.
FS_TITLE=Root filesystem
FS_TEXT=Choose the filesystem for the Sinux root partition.
FS_EXT2=ext2 (recommended - readable by the Sinux ext2 driver)
FS_EXT4=ext4 (GRUB can boot it, Sinux kernel cannot read it)
HOST_TITLE=Hostname
HOST_TEXT=Enter a hostname for the installed system.
PLAN_TITLE=Installation plan
PLAN_OK=Start the installation now?
STEP_PART=Creating GPT partition table
STEP_FORMAT=Formatting EFI and root partitions
STEP_COPY=Copying Sinux kernel and system files
STEP_BIOS=Installing GRUB for legacy BIOS
STEP_UEFI=Installing GRUB for UEFI
STEP_DONE=Writing boot configuration and finishing
DRY_TITLE=Dry run
DRY_TEXT=DRY RUN: no disk was modified. The planned commands are shown in the log.
DONE_TITLE=Installation complete
DONE_TEXT=Sinux was installed successfully.\n\nRemove the installation media before rebooting.\nOn real hardware: disable Secure Boot, then boot the disk in BIOS or UEFI mode.\n\nThe Sinux kernel boots into its own built-in terminal shell.
ERR_TITLE=Error
CANCELLED=Operation cancelled. No changes were made.
YES_LABEL=Yes
NO_LABEL=No
OK_LABEL=OK
BACK_LABEL=Back
REBOOT_Q=Reboot now?
SHELL_TITLE=Rescue shell
SHELL_TEXT=Starting a bash rescue shell. Type 'exit' to return to the installer.
SELFTEST=Self-test / automated mode
MEDIA_NOTE=Note: the installation media itself is excluded from the disk list.
PRESS_ENTER=Press Enter to continue.
INSTALL_LOG=Installer log
NO_DEVICE=No target disk was selected.
BAD_DEVICE=The selected device is not a valid block disk.
FIRMWARE_BIOS=Detected firmware: legacy BIOS
FIRMWARE_UEFI=Detected firmware: UEFI
ACT_DRYRUN=Dry run (no changes)
DRY_NOTE=Show the plan without touching the disk.
LOG_SAVED=A copy of the log was saved on the installed system at /etc/sinux/install.log
REBOOT_TITLE=Ready to boot into Sinux
REBOOT_HINT=Installation is complete and the live system runs entirely from RAM.\n\nUnplug the installation USB stick NOW, then press OK.\n\nThe machine reboots automatically and the installed Sinux terminal appears. If you leave the USB stick in, the installer menu detects the installed system and boots it anyway.
REBOOT_FAILED=The reboot did not happen. Power the machine off, remove the installation USB stick, then turn it on again.
